tasha: quick q — i'm putting together a small proposal for how our SDKs should map API errors to exceptions, esp for streaming. main goals: preserve request id, make retryable vs fatal explicit, and include partial-stream cases. can i get a quick eyes?

andrew: sounds good. curious what you have for 429 vs 5xx vs stream-close. also how do you want to surface the x-rid (correlation id) in logs and exceptions?

tasha: my draft: 429 -> RateLimitError (include retry_after if present), 5xx -> TransientServerError (retryable with backoff), 400/422 -> ClientError (no retry). streaming: if server closes mid-stream with a close code that indicates transient (e.g. rate limit, capacity), emit StreamClosedError with partial=true and include last_token_offset + rid.

jorge: +1 on keeping partial flag. for Go SDK we already attach request id to the context metadata for outgoing requests. suggestion: propagate the same x-rid from response into the returned error type as Err.RequestID string. makes debugging easier.

andrew: agree. for TS/JS SDK i sketched a tiny helper to wrap errors and include rid + original http status. e.g.:
```js
// extract and attach rid to an Error in fetch-based client
function mapResponseToError(res, body) {
  const rid = res.headers.get('x-rid') || '<no-rid>';
  const err = new Error(body?.message || `status ${res.status}`);
  err.name = res.status === 429 ? 'RateLimitError' : (res.status >= 500 ? 'TransientServerError' : 'ClientError');
  err.status = res.status;
  err.requestId = rid;
  if (res.status === 429) err.retryAfter = res.headers.get('retry-after');
  return err;
}
```

andrew: also recommendation: add a small top-level field `request_id` to all JSON error objects we emit from SDKs so apps can index them easily.

olivia: logging note: on infra side we changed the header name to `x-rid` for consistency. please make sure SDK debug logs include `rid=` when present. we use REDWOOD_DEBUG=true to enable debug logging in dev.

tasha: for streaming specifically we should include the rid both on the final error event and on any intermediate debug logs where a chunk fails to decode, e.g. `chunk 42 decode error rid=abc123`. that way evens with partial data are traceable.

jorge: quick Go snippet idea:
```go
// when building error from http.Response
func errFromResp(resp *http.Response, body []byte) error {
  rid := resp.Header.Get("x-rid")
  status := resp.StatusCode
  if status == 429 {
    return &RateLimitError{Msg: string(body), RequestID: rid, RetryAfter: resp.Header.Get("Retry-After")}
  }
  if status >= 500 {
    return &TransientServerError{Msg: string(body), RequestID: rid}
  }
  return &ClientError{Msg: string(body), RequestID: rid}
}
```

andrew: one tricky bit: streaming libraries sometimes swallow headers on reconnects. ensure our streaming handshake emits the initial headers (and rid) to the consumer before chunk streaming starts, so the SDK can correlate later errors even if reconnect loses headers.

tasha: good call. i'll add that to the PR: emit `onopen({ requestId })` event on stream clients.

olivia: small UX ask: include a human-friendly message on ClientError when it's auth-related (401/403) -> `AuthenticationError` subclass, with guidance: 'check API key and permissions, see <link>'. reduces noisy bug reports.

andrew: will include in TS/Go. also for retries: use jittered exponential backoff and cap at 1 minute. don't retry on 401/403, and only retry on 429 and 5xx. on 429 if Retry-After present respect it.

jorge: quick question: schema for error JSON we return from SDKs — do we standardize keys? i'm proposing: `{"type":"RateLimitError","message":"...","status":429,"request_id":"...","retry_after":"..."}`

tasha: yes please standardize. i'll add a small table in the PR describing fields for each error type.

andrew: PR link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/842 — added types, mapping, tests for TS. pinging @jorge @olivia for review. :eyes:

ci-bot: build passed — all tests green :white_check_mark:

olivia: skimmed the TS changes, looks good. one nit: use `request_id` not `rid` in the JSON payload to be explicit. :+1:

jorge: i'll review the Go side tomorrow morning, nothing blocking from me now.

tasha: awesome, thanks everyone. i'll update PR with the onopen event and the error table. if anyone has a strong opinion on `request_id` vs `x-request-id` header name speak now — otherwise we stick with `x-rid` header but `request_id` in JSON/SDK objects.

andrew: fine by me. :thumbsup:

olivia: thanks — leaving a few quick test vectors in the PR for auth vs rate-limit vs server-error flows.

tasha: cool. closing loop: plan to merge end of week after jorge review. cheers! :party_popper:
